export const PRIVACY_HTML = "<h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p><strong>Last updated: 23 September 2026</strong></p><p>WorkRoute (“we”, “us”, “our”) respects your privacy and is committed to protecting personal information.</p><p>This Privacy Policy explains how WorkRoute collects, uses, stores and protects personal information when you visit our website, create an account, use the WorkRoute service, contact us, or otherwise interact with us.</p><hr><h2>1. Information We Collect</h2><p>Depending on how you use WorkRoute, we may collect personal information including:</p><h3>Information you provide to us</h3><ul><li><p>Name</p></li><li><p>Business name</p></li><li><p>Email address</p></li><li><p>Phone number</p></li><li><p>Trade or business type</p></li><li><p>Business and service-area information</p></li><li><p>Account and login information</p></li><li><p>Billing and subscription information</p></li><li><p>Information you provide when contacting us or requesting support</p></li></ul><h3>Information relating to customers and jobs</h3><p>When you use WorkRoute to manage your business, you may enter information relating to your customers and jobs, including:</p><ul><li><p>Customer names</p></li><li><p>Customer phone numbers and email addresses</p></li><li><p>Customer addresses and service locations</p></li><li><p>Job descriptions and requirements</p></li><li><p>Appointment dates and times</p></li><li><p>Recurring job information</p></li><li><p>Customer communications and messages</p></li><li><p>Job notes and scheduling information</p></li><li><p>Route and location information relevant to performing jobs</p></li><li><p>Before-and-after photographs</p></li><li><p>Voice notes and job-related recordings</p></li><li><p>Invoice and payment-status information</p></li></ul><p>You are responsible for ensuring that you have the appropriate authority to provide WorkRoute with personal information relating to your customers.</p><p>Please do not provide WorkRoute with sensitive personal information unless it is reasonably necessary for the service and you are legally entitled to provide it.</p><hr><h2>2. How We Collect Personal Information</h2><p>We may collect personal information:</p><ul><li><p>Directly from you when you create or use a WorkRoute account</p></li><li><p>When you contact us</p></li><li><p>When you enter customer or job information into WorkRoute</p></li><li><p>Through forms on our website</p></li><li><p>Through your use of WorkRoute features</p></li><li><p>Through phone, SMS, messaging and other communications used as part of the service</p></li><li><p>From third-party services or integrations that you choose to connect to WorkRoute</p></li></ul><p>We may also automatically collect certain technical information when you use our website or service, including information such as your IP address, browser type, device information, operating system and information about how the website or service is used.</p><hr><h2>3. How We Use Personal Information</h2><p>We may collect, hold, use and disclose personal information to:</p><ul><li><p>Provide and operate WorkRoute</p></li><li><p>Manage customer enquiries and bookings</p></li><li><p>Assist with scheduling and route planning</p></li><li><p>Manage recurring jobs</p></li><li><p>Send booking confirmations and service notifications</p></li><li><p>Provide phone, SMS, messaging and other communication functions</p></li><li><p>Provide AI-assisted office and scheduling functions</p></li><li><p>Create and maintain customer and job records</p></li><li><p>Generate job summaries, invoices and other business records</p></li><li><p>Provide customer review and follow-up features</p></li><li><p>Process WorkRoute subscriptions and payments</p></li><li><p>Respond to enquiries and provide customer support</p></li><li><p>Maintain, secure and improve WorkRoute</p></li><li><p>Detect and prevent fraud, misuse or security incidents</p></li><li><p>Comply with legal and regulatory obligations</p></li></ul><p>We do not sell or rent personal information.</p><hr><h2>4. Artificial Intelligence and Automated Processing</h2><p>WorkRoute uses artificial intelligence and automated systems to provide features such as customer enquiry handling, booking assistance, scheduling, route planning, communications, job summaries and other administrative functions.</p><p>AI-generated or automated outputs may be based on information you provide, customer information, business rules, schedules and other relevant service information.</p><p>AI systems can make mistakes. Automated outputs should be reviewed where accuracy is important.</p><p>WorkRoute does not currently intend to use personal information to make decisions that have a significant effect on an individual in circumstances where human involvement is required by applicable law.</p><p>Where WorkRoute introduces automated decision-making that is subject to additional privacy requirements, we will update this Privacy Policy and provide any information required by applicable law.</p><hr><h2>5. Communications</h2><p>WorkRoute may use email, SMS, telephone, messaging and other communication services to provide the service and communicate with you.</p><p>This may include:</p><ul><li><p>Account and service notifications</p></li><li><p>Booking confirmations</p></li><li><p>Appointment and scheduling communications</p></li><li><p>Customer communications configured by you</p></li><li><p>Customer support communications</p></li><li><p>Important service announcements</p></li><li><p>Marketing communications where permitted by law</p></li></ul><p>You are responsible for ensuring that you have the necessary authority and permissions to use WorkRoute to contact your customers.</p><p>Where consent is required for marketing communications, WorkRoute will provide an appropriate way to withdraw that consent.</p><hr><h2>6. Payments and Billing</h2><p>WorkRoute uses third-party payment providers to process subscription payments.</p><p>Payment information may be collected and processed directly by the payment provider. WorkRoute may receive information such as transaction references, payment status, subscription status and other information required to administer your account.</p><p>Where payment details are collected directly by a third-party payment provider, WorkRoute does not intend to store full credit card or bank account details.</p><p>Our payment providers may have their own privacy policies and terms.</p><hr><h2>7. Third-Party Service Providers and Integrations</h2><p>WorkRoute relies on third-party providers to help operate and deliver the service.</p><p>These may include providers for:</p><ul><li><p>Website and cloud hosting</p></li><li><p>Databases and data storage</p></li><li><p>Artificial intelligence</p></li><li><p>Telecommunications and voice services</p></li><li><p>SMS and messaging</p></li><li><p>Mapping and route services</p></li><li><p>Payment processing</p></li><li><p>Email and communications</p></li><li><p>Analytics and website performance</p></li><li><p>Accounting integrations</p></li><li><p>Automation and software integrations</p></li></ul><p>Third-party providers may process personal information on our behalf where reasonably necessary to provide their services.</p><p>Where you connect a third-party service or integration, WorkRoute may exchange information reasonably required to provide that integration.</p><p>Third-party services may operate or store information outside Australia. Where applicable and practicable, WorkRoute will identify relevant overseas recipients or locations through this Privacy Policy or other appropriate notices.</p><p>Third-party providers are responsible for their own systems, policies and privacy practices.</p><hr><h2>8. How We Hold and Protect Personal Information</h2><p>We take reasonable steps to protect personal information from:</p><ul><li><p>Misuse</p></li><li><p>Interference</p></li><li><p>Loss</p></li><li><p>Unauthorised access</p></li><li><p>Unauthorised modification</p></li><li><p>Unauthorised disclosure</p></li></ul><p>Personal information may be stored electronically using WorkRoute systems and trusted third-party service providers.</p><p>Access is limited to people and providers who reasonably need access for legitimate business or service purposes.</p><p>No method of electronic storage or transmission is completely secure. Where a privacy or security incident occurs, WorkRoute will take reasonable steps to contain, investigate and respond to it and comply with applicable legal requirements.</p><p>Where applicable, WorkRoute will comply with the Australian Notifiable Data Breaches scheme.</p><hr><h2>9. Data Retention and Deletion</h2><p>We retain personal information for as long as reasonably necessary to:</p><ul><li><p>Provide the WorkRoute service</p></li><li><p>Maintain business and transaction records</p></li><li><p>Provide customer support</p></li><li><p>Resolve disputes and complaints</p></li><li><p>Meet legal or regulatory obligations</p></li><li><p>Protect the security and integrity of WorkRoute</p></li></ul><p>When personal information is no longer reasonably required, we may securely delete or de-identify it, subject to legal, accounting, security or other legitimate retention requirements.</p><p>After an account is cancelled, information may remain in backups or records for a reasonable period before deletion or de-identification.</p><hr><h2>10. Cookies and Analytics</h2><p>WorkRoute may use cookies, analytics and similar technologies to:</p><ul><li><p>Keep our website and service functioning</p></li><li><p>Understand how visitors use our website</p></li><li><p>Improve performance and user experience</p></li><li><p>Monitor security and prevent misuse</p></li></ul><p>You can control or disable cookies through your browser settings. Some features may not function correctly if certain cookies are disabled.</p><hr><h2>11. Access and Correction</h2><p>You may request access to personal information we hold about you.</p><p>You may also ask us to correct personal information that is inaccurate, incomplete or out of date.</p><p>We may need to verify your identity before providing access to or changing personal information.</p><p>To make a request, contact us using the details below.</p><hr><h2>12. Privacy Complaints</h2><p>If you believe WorkRoute has handled your personal information in a way that does not comply with applicable privacy laws, you may make a privacy complaint by contacting us.</p><p>Please provide enough information for us to understand and investigate your complaint.</p><p>We will review privacy complaints and respond within a reasonable period.</p><p>If you are not satisfied with our response, or your complaint is not resolved, you may contact the <strong>Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC)</strong>.</p><hr><h2>13. Your Responsibilities When Using WorkRoute</h2><p>Where you enter or upload information about your own customers into WorkRoute, you are responsible for ensuring that:</p><ul><li><p>You have the authority to provide that information to WorkRoute</p></li><li><p>Your collection and use of customer information complies with applicable laws</p></li><li><p>You provide any privacy notices or obtain any consents required by law</p></li><li><p>You use WorkRoute’s communication features lawfully</p></li></ul><p>WorkRoute acts as a technology service provider for these business functions and does not replace your own privacy obligations.</p><hr><h2>14. Overseas Disclosure</h2><p>Some technology providers used by WorkRoute may store or process information outside Australia.</p><p>The countries in which information may be processed can depend on the providers and services used at the time.</p><p>Where practicable, WorkRoute will identify relevant overseas recipients or countries in this Privacy Policy or through other appropriate notices.</p><hr><h2>15. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2><p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes to WorkRoute, our information-handling practices, third-party services or applicable legal requirements.</p><p>The latest version will be published on our website and will show the date it was last updated.</p><hr><h2>16. Contact Us</h2><p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, want to request access to or correction of your personal information, or wish to make a privacy complaint, please contact us at:</p><p><strong>Email:</strong><a href=\"mailto:steve@workroute.com.au\">steve@workroute.com.au</a><br><strong>Business name:</strong> WorkRoute<br><strong>Country:</strong> Australia</p>";

export const TERMS_HTML = "<h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1><p><strong>Effective date: 23 September 2026</strong></p><h2>1. About these Terms</h2><p>These Terms &amp; Conditions (\"Terms\") apply to your access to and use of WorkRoute, including the WorkRoute website, application, AI Office Manager, communications tools, scheduling and route-planning tools, customer records, job management, invoicing tools, integrations and related services (together, the \"Service\").</p><p>In these Terms, \"WorkRoute\", \"we\", \"us\" and \"our\" means the operator of the WorkRoute service. \"You\" and \"your\" means the business or person using the Service and, where applicable, the people authorised by that business to use it.</p><p>By creating an account, starting a trial, subscribing to the Service or otherwise using the Service, you agree to these Terms.</p><h2>2. The WorkRoute Service</h2><p>WorkRoute is an AI-powered office and job-management platform designed to help trade and service businesses manage customer enquiries, bookings, schedules, routes, job records, communications and administration.</p><p>Depending on your plan and configuration, WorkRoute may provide:</p><ul><li>AI phone answering and customer enquiry handling;</li><li>AI-generated or business-configured quotes and pricing responses;</li><li>website chat and customer messaging;</li><li>customer SMS and notifications;</li><li>customer and returning-caller recognition;</li><li>booking, availability and recurring-job management;</li><li>route planning and calculated travel information;</li><li>\"On My Way\" and delay notifications;</li><li>customer records, notes and job history;</li><li>before-and-after job photographs;</li><li>voice job notes and automatic job summaries;</li><li>numbered invoice generation and invoice delivery;</li><li>invoice follow-up and payment-status features;</li><li>Google review requests and customer win-back features;</li><li>daily business and weather information;</li><li>kilometre records between jobs;</li><li>an installable phone application and notifications; and</li><li>optional integrations with services such as Xero, MYOB, QuickBooks and Zapier.</li></ul><p>Features may change over time as WorkRoute is developed. We may add, remove, improve or modify features provided that doing so does not unlawfully remove rights that apply to you.</p><h2>3. Your account</h2><p>You must provide accurate information when creating and maintaining your account. You are responsible for keeping your login credentials secure and for all activity carried out through your account.</p><p>You must tell us promptly if you believe your account has been accessed without permission.</p><p>You are responsible for ensuring that people using WorkRoute on behalf of your business are authorised to do so and comply with these Terms.</p><h2>4. Sign-up, subscription, pricing and payment</h2><p>WorkRoute subscriptions are purchased through <strong>app.workroute.com.au</strong>. By creating an account, completing the signup process and accepting these Terms during signup, you agree to be bound by these Terms.</p><p>WorkRoute is offered as a paid subscription service. Unless a different price is displayed or agreed at signup, the advertised WorkRoute subscription is <strong>AUD $199 per month</strong>.</p><p>Unless a different arrangement is expressly agreed with you, your WorkRoute subscription is <strong>month-to-month with no minimum contract period or lock-in</strong>. You may cancel at any time in accordance with these Terms.</p><p>Your subscription is billed on a recurring basis using the payment method you provide. Before recurring billing begins, you will be provided with the applicable subscription price and billing terms and will be required to authorise the recurring payment arrangement through WorkRoute's payment provider.</p><p>The payment provider may process payments on behalf of WorkRoute and may provide WorkRoute with payment status, transaction and subscription information necessary to administer your WorkRoute account.</p><p>If a payment fails, WorkRoute or its payment provider may notify you and may attempt to process the payment again in accordance with the provider's procedures. You are responsible for maintaining a valid payment method and sufficient funds to meet amounts due.</p><p>If an amount remains unpaid, WorkRoute may suspend or restrict access to the Service until the account is brought up to date. Suspension for non-payment does not cancel amounts already owed.</p><p>If a free trial or promotional offer is available, the applicable trial period, eligibility and any conditions will be shown at signup. Unless you cancel before the trial ends where cancellation is required, the subscription may convert to the applicable paid subscription.</p><p>WorkRoute does not require you to purchase individual WorkRoute feature subscriptions where the advertised plan states that features are included. Third-party services and their own charges may be separate.</p><h2>6. Free trials and promotional offers</h2><p>Where WorkRoute offers a free trial, only one trial may be available per eligible business or account unless we expressly agree otherwise. We may change or withdraw a trial or promotion at any time before it is accepted.</p><p>Trial users receive access to the features stated in the applicable offer. We do not guarantee that a trial will continue for any particular period if the offer contains conditions that have not been met.</p><h2>7. AI Office Manager and automated actions</h2><p>WorkRoute uses artificial intelligence and automation to assist with customer communications, enquiries, quoting, booking, scheduling, route planning, job records and other administrative tasks.</p><p>AI systems can make mistakes. WorkRoute does not guarantee that every AI-generated response, quote, transcription, booking, route recommendation, customer record or other output will be complete or accurate.</p><p>You remain responsible for your business decisions and for checking important information where appropriate, including pricing, availability, service areas, booking details, customer instructions, job requirements and invoices.</p><p>You authorise WorkRoute to perform the automated actions that you configure it to perform. You should configure your business rules, pricing, service areas, availability and other settings carefully.</p><p>Where a customer interacts with an AI system, WorkRoute may identify the interaction as AI-assisted or automated where required or appropriate.</p><h2>8. Quotes and pricing</h2><p>Where WorkRoute provides pricing or quote functionality, the figures are generated from the information, pricing rules and business settings supplied or approved by you, together with the information available to WorkRoute at the time.</p><p>You are responsible for ensuring your pricing, inclusions, exclusions, travel charges, minimum charges and other commercial rules are accurate and up to date.</p><p>WorkRoute does not guarantee that an AI-generated quote will be appropriate for every property, job or circumstance.</p><h2>9. Bookings, availability and recurring jobs</h2><p>WorkRoute may assist with checking availability, booking jobs, managing recurring visits and organising a daily run.</p><p>You remain responsible for ensuring that the business information used by WorkRoute is accurate, including working hours, availability, service areas, job durations, travel assumptions, pricing and staff or vehicle availability.</p><p>WorkRoute may use travel-time and routing information to help avoid impractical schedules, but actual travel conditions can change. Traffic, road closures, weather, access issues and other circumstances may affect arrival times.</p><h2>10. Route planning and ETA information</h2><p>WorkRoute may use mapping and routing services to calculate routes and estimated travel times.</p><p>Route and ETA information is an estimate only and is not a guarantee of arrival time. You remain responsible for safe driving, lawful road use and deciding whether a proposed route is suitable.</p><p>\"On My Way\" and similar customer messages are intended to provide an estimated arrival time based on available routing information. They are not intended to provide continuous live tracking of the tradie.</p><h2>11. Customer communications</h2><p>WorkRoute may send or assist with sending phone calls, SMS messages, website chat messages, email messages, Messenger messages, review requests and other customer communications depending on your configuration.</p><p>You are responsible for ensuring that you have the necessary authority, permissions and consents to contact your customers and to use their personal information for the purposes for which you configure WorkRoute.</p><p>You must not use WorkRoute to send unlawful, misleading, harassing, abusive, deceptive or unsolicited communications.</p><p>You are responsible for complying with applicable Australian rules relating to privacy, spam, telemarketing, consent and customer communications.</p><h2>12. Customer data and your content</h2><p>You may provide WorkRoute with information about your business, customers, jobs, addresses, phone numbers, notes, photographs, messages, recordings, invoices and other information (\"Customer Data\").</p><p>You retain your rights in Customer Data. You grant WorkRoute the limited rights necessary to host, process, transmit, store and use Customer Data to provide, secure, maintain and improve the Service and as otherwise permitted by your instructions and applicable law.</p><p>You are responsible for ensuring that you have the right to provide Customer Data to WorkRoute and that your collection and use of Customer Data complies with applicable privacy and other laws.</p><p>WorkRoute will handle personal information in accordance with its Privacy Policy, which forms part of the overall terms governing use of the Service.</p><h2>13. Privacy</h2><p>Our Privacy Policy explains how WorkRoute collects, uses, stores and protects personal information.</p><p>You should read the Privacy Policy before using the Service. You are also responsible for providing appropriate privacy notices to your own customers where required.</p><h2>14. Voice notes, photographs and job records</h2><p>WorkRoute may allow you to create job records from voice notes and photographs. Automated processing may be used to turn your input into summaries, job history, invoice information or other records.</p><p>You are responsible for reviewing important records before relying on them where accuracy is important.</p><p>Before-and-after photographs are a record-keeping tool. They do not constitute insurance, legal advice, a guarantee against disputes or a guarantee that a claim will be rejected.</p><h2>15. Invoices and payments from your customers</h2><p>WorkRoute may generate numbered invoices and assist with sending them to your customers.</p><p>Unless a separate payment service is enabled, WorkRoute does not itself collect your customers' cash or bank-transfer payments. Your customer may pay you by the payment methods you specify, such as cash on completion or bank transfer using the bank details shown on your invoice.</p><p>You are responsible for checking invoice details, tax treatment, business bank details, amounts owing and payment status before relying on an invoice.</p><p>Optional accounting integrations may transfer information between WorkRoute and third-party accounting services. Those services are subject to their own terms and privacy policies.</p><h2>16. Kilometre records</h2><p>WorkRoute may record kilometres or travel information between jobs for business record-keeping purposes.</p><p>These records are a supporting record only and are not represented as an official ATO logbook or tax determination. You are responsible for maintaining whatever tax and vehicle records you are legally required to keep.</p><h2>17. Third-party services and integrations</h2><p>WorkRoute may integrate with or rely on third-party services, including mapping, telecommunications, SMS, AI, email, payment, accounting, automation and other technology providers.</p><p>Third-party services are outside WorkRoute's direct control. Their availability, pricing, features, limits, policies and terms may change.</p><p>Where you connect a third-party service, you authorise WorkRoute to exchange the information reasonably required to provide the integration you have enabled.</p><p>WorkRoute is not responsible for a third party's independent service failure, outage, pricing change, account suspension, data loss or policy change.</p><h2>18. Customer reviews and win-back communications</h2><p>WorkRoute may help request Google reviews or contact previous customers where those features are enabled.</p><p>You are responsible for ensuring that review requests, marketing communications and win-back communications comply with applicable laws and the terms of the relevant third-party platform.</p><p>WorkRoute does not guarantee that a customer will leave a review, return for another job or respond to a communication.</p><h2>19. Your responsibilities</h2><p>You must:</p><ul><li>use WorkRoute lawfully and in accordance with these Terms;</li><li>provide accurate business, pricing, availability and customer information;</li><li>keep your account and access credentials secure;</li><li>obtain required customer permissions and consents;</li><li>review important AI-generated outputs where appropriate;</li><li>ensure your use of WorkRoute does not infringe another person's rights; and</li><li>maintain appropriate backups or copies of information you need to retain.</li></ul><h2>20. Prohibited use</h2><p>You must not use WorkRoute to:</p><ul><li>break the law or facilitate unlawful activity;</li><li>send spam, scams, threats or deceptive communications;</li><li>impersonate another person or business;</li><li>upload malicious code or attempt to compromise the Service;</li><li>interfere with the Service or attempt unauthorised access;</li><li>reverse engineer or copy the Service except where the law expressly permits it;</li><li>use the Service to process information you do not have a lawful right to provide; or</li><li>use WorkRoute in a way that could reasonably harm WorkRoute, its providers or other users.</li></ul><h2>21. WorkRoute intellectual property</h2><p>WorkRoute and its software, design, branding, systems, workflows, documentation and underlying technology are owned by or licensed to WorkRoute and are protected by applicable intellectual property laws.</p><p>Subject to these Terms, WorkRoute grants you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the Service during your active subscription for your internal business purposes.</p><p>You must not copy, resell, lease, sublicense or commercially exploit the WorkRoute platform itself unless we expressly agree in writing.</p><h2>22. Availability and changes to the Service</h2><p>We aim to keep WorkRoute available and reliable, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation.</p><p>The Service may occasionally be unavailable because of maintenance, upgrades, security incidents, telecommunications problems, third-party outages or circumstances outside our reasonable control.</p><p>We may update or change the Service as technology, security requirements and business needs evolve.</p><h2>23. Suspension or termination by WorkRoute</h2><p>We may suspend or terminate access to the Service if you materially breach these Terms, fail to pay amounts due, misuse the Service, create a security risk, or where suspension or termination is reasonably necessary to comply with law or protect the Service or other users.</p><p>Where reasonably practicable, we will provide notice and an opportunity to remedy a breach before suspension or termination, unless immediate action is reasonably required.</p><h2>24. Data after cancellation</h2><p>After your subscription ends, your access to the Service may be disabled. We may retain or delete account and Customer Data in accordance with our Privacy Policy, legal obligations, legitimate business needs and our applicable data-retention practices.</p><p>You are responsible for exporting or retaining information you need before cancelling your account where the Service provides an export or download facility.</p><h2>25. Disclaimers</h2><p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, WorkRoute is provided as a business software service and is not a substitute for your own professional judgement, supervision or responsibility.</p><p>We do not guarantee that WorkRoute will:</p><ul><li>increase revenue or reduce costs;</li><li>prevent missed calls or lost leads in every circumstance;</li><li>produce error-free AI responses;</li><li>calculate every route or ETA perfectly;</li><li>avoid every scheduling conflict;</li><li>produce tax-compliant records for every situation; or</li><li>ensure that every customer communication, quote, invoice or job record is correct without review.</li></ul><p>Nothing in these Terms excludes a guarantee, condition, right or remedy that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p><h2>26. Limitation of liability</h2><p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, WorkRoute will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss, loss of profits, loss of revenue, loss of business opportunity, loss of goodwill or loss of data arising from your use of the Service.</p><p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, WorkRoute's total liability arising out of or relating to the Service will be limited to the amount you paid to WorkRoute for the Service during the twelve months immediately before the event giving rise to the claim.</p><p>This section does not exclude or limit liability where doing so would be unlawful.</p><h2>27. Indemnity</h2><p>To the extent permitted by law, you agree to indemnify WorkRoute against claims, losses, liabilities, costs and expenses arising from your unlawful use of the Service, your breach of these Terms, your failure to obtain required customer permissions, or your infringement of another person's rights.</p><h2>28. Force majeure</h2><p>WorkRoute will not be responsible for delay or failure caused by events outside our reasonable control, including telecommunications failures, internet outages, third-party service failures, natural disasters, severe weather, cyber incidents, government action, industrial disputes or other events that could not reasonably be prevented or avoided.</p><h2>29. Changes to these Terms</h2><p>We may update these Terms from time to time. When we make a material change, we may provide notice through the Service or another reasonable method.</p><p>Your continued use of WorkRoute after updated Terms take effect constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms, to the extent permitted by law.</p><h2>30. Governing law</h2><p>These Terms are governed by the laws of Queensland, Australia, except to the extent another law must apply.</p><p>You and WorkRoute submit to the courts of Queensland, Australia, and courts entitled to hear appeals from them, subject to any mandatory rights or jurisdictional requirements that apply under Australian law.</p><h2>31. Australian Consumer Law</h2><p>Nothing in these Terms is intended to exclude, restrict or modify rights or remedies available under the Australian Consumer Law or any other applicable law.</p><p>Australian businesses and consumers may have statutory rights that cannot be excluded by contract. WorkRoute will comply with those rights where they apply.</p><h2>32. General</h2><p>If any provision of these Terms is found to be invalid or unenforceable, that provision will be read down or severed to the extent necessary and the remaining provisions will continue to operate.</p><p>A failure or delay by WorkRoute to enforce a provision does not constitute a waiver of that provision.</p><p>These Terms, together with the Privacy Policy and any specific subscription or service terms shown to you at signup, form the agreement between you and WorkRoute concerning the Service.</p><h2>33. Contact</h2><p>If you have a question, complaint or request concerning these Terms or the WorkRoute Service, please use the contact details published on the WorkRoute website.</p><p>If you have a complaint about WorkRoute, including a subscription, payment, refund, account or Service issue, please contact us using the contact details published on the WorkRoute website. We will review the complaint and respond within a reasonable period.</p><p>Where a matter relates to a third-party payment provider, we may work with that provider as necessary to investigate and resolve the issue.</p> © 2026 WorkRoute. All rights reserved.";
